### Ran Playwright code
```js
await page.evaluate('() => ({w:window.__FF3D.player.weapons, firing:window.__FF3D.player.firing, inputFiring:window.__FF3D.input.firing, reload:window.__FF3D.player.reloading, stats:window.__FF3D.stats})');
```

### Result
{
  "fps": 4
}
### Ran Playwright code
```js
await page.evaluate('() => new Promise(res=>{let n=0;const t=performance.now();const f=()=>{n++;if(performance.now()-t<1000)requestAnimationFrame(f);else res({fps:n})};requestAnimationFrame(f)})');
```

4 fps software. Need optimize maybe significant; screenshots still possible. Real GPU likely 60fps. But we should reduce load for SwiftShader and mobile. Could lower shadow map 1024, reduce terrain segments 150x150 = 45k tris (90k tris? 150*150*2=45k triangles). Fine. Draw calls main cost. Many tree meshes 78*4=312 draw calls + shadows. Could merge static geometry by material? Complex. But can use `BufferGeometryUtils.mergeGeometries` grouped by material? Or InstancedMesh. Performance 4fps under software maybe acceptable for CI screenshot but game should be playable on real hardware. Still, 500 draw calls + shadows can be heavy on mobile. We can optimize trees using instancing or merged geometries.

Given user wants complete playable game, performance important. Let's at least disable shadows on mobile? and reduce shadow map to 1024. Also the water plane with 700x700 and tons? no.

Draw calls include ~30 buildings * maybe 10 meshes = 300, containers ~60 ribs, trees ~300, bushes 110, rocks 34, clouds 12, gulls 16, loot ~50 each 3 = 150. Total ~1000 draw calls. That's high. Need optimize.

Options:
1. Merge static meshes by material after world creation. All world static except zone, water. Could traverse scene and merge meshes sharing material into merged geometry. But colliders independent. We can implement `mergeStaticMeshes(scene)` using BufferGeometryUtils.mergeGeometries. Need preserve transforms. Group by material UUID and castShadow/receiveShadow flags. But meshes with distinct geometries and materials can be merged. Some are emissive (windows), etc. We can merge each material separately. Materials count maybe 30. This reduces draw calls massively (per material per shadow flag). However merging requires geometry attributes consistent (position, normal, uv). Rounded boxes/cylinders all have uv, normal; ours mostly boxes/cylinders/cones/spheres? All have uv/normal. Vertex color terrain excluded because distinct material and huge. Could include static only before loot/bots. We can mark world group? Currently world objects added directly to scene. We could modify createWorld to put all world groups in a `worldGroup` and then merge. More work but doable. Alternatively perform merge inside createWorld at end by traversing scene excluding water/terrain/zone/clouds/gulls. But all these merged would kill animation of clouds/water/gulls. We can create a root group `staticGroup` for static props and merge children.

Better modify world.js: create `const staticRoot = new THREE.Group(); scene.add(staticRoot);` and pass staticRoot as scene to building/tree/etc. Then at end call mergeStatic(staticRoot) using BufferGeometryUtils. Zone/water/terrain/clouds remain scene. Need import mergeGeometries from 'three/addons/utils/BufferGeometryUtils.js'. Merge by material and castShadow/receiveShadow. But some static meshes have rotated transformations; merge applies world matrices. Good.

However merging all can break frustum culling (single huge island mesh draws even when offscreen) but still fewer draw calls. Shadow rendering also fewer. Big win.

Let's implement `mergeStatic`:
```
function mergeStaticGroup(root) {
 const buckets=new Map();
 root.updateMatrixWorld(true);
 root.traverse(o=>{ if(!o.isMesh) return; const key = o.material.uuid + '|' + o.castShadow + '|' + o.receiveShadow; ... clone geometry applyMatrix4(o.matrixWorld); push;});
 // remove original root children
 while(root.children.length) root.remove(root.children[0]);
 for each bucket: const merged=mergeGeometries(geoms,false); const mesh=new Mesh(merged, material); cast/receive; root.add(mesh);
}
```
- Need geometries have same attributes: BoxGeometry, CylinderGeometry, ConeGeometry, IcosahedronGeometry, SphereGeometry, RingGeometry, PlaneGeometry all position/normal/uv. Good.
- Some may have groups with multi-material? No.
- Transforming geometry with non-uniform scale is applied, normals need normalMatrix: applyMatrix4 handles normal transform.
- Dispose old geometries after merging.
- Since we merge by material, texture etc preserved.
